# Copy this file to `config` beside it and fill it in. `config` is ignored
# by version control: it names your server, and your server is not the
# repository's business.

# The server, as ssh itself takes it: user@address, user@hostname, or a
# Host alias from your own ssh config. A Tailscale name (user@myserver)
# reaches the server from any network, not only its own.
SERVER="user@host"

# How often the watch script asks the server again, in seconds. Leave it
# empty for the default, which the watch window shows as its refresh rate.
REFRESH_SECONDS=""

# Which tmux sessions to show, by their tmux names, separated by spaces.
# Empty shows every tmux session the server keeps running — on a server
# shared with others, name yours here and see only those.
TMUX_SESSIONS=""

# Whether the sessions folder numbers its files in the order the sessions
# were started: "001 notes", "002 recipes", and so on. The number moves up
# when an older session ends, and is only ever in the file's name — the tmux
# session keeps the name you gave it. Anything but "true", or the key left
# out, names each file after its session alone.
NUMBER_SESSIONS="true"

# The server's name in Tailscale, when it is reached that way: its
# machine name, its full ts.net name, or its 100.x address. Lets the tool
# say why a link is lost, and check the server before a trip. Empty means
# Tailscale is never asked anything.
TAILSCALE_NODE=""
